      "cemetery_location": "",
      "full_text": "She is survived by two sisters, Alice Dean of Quinton Twp. and Pauline Pierce \n  of Dover, DE and several nieces and nephews. She was preceded in death by her \n  brother Norman Cuff and her brother in law, William Dean.",
      "source_url": "https://nativeamericansofdelawarestate.com/Obituaries%20added%202016-04-03.htm"
    },
    {
      "person_id": 247,
      "id": 210,
      "deceased_name": "Ethelda \"Ted\" Street Dean",
      "age": "86",
      "birth_date": "",
      "death_date": "2006",
      "cemetery_location": "",
      "full_text": "Ethelda \"Ted\" Street Dean Age 86, departed this life Aug. 7, 2006 \n at Parkview Nursing Center. Beloved wife of William Dean. Loving mother of Ron \n Dean & his wife, Julie Sertel, and stepson, Richard Spencer. Grandmother \n of Ella & Anthony Dean. Sister of Gladys Porter, of Ann Arbor, MI, & \n the late Evelyn Gardner Green (Kenneth). Also survived by many nieces, nephews, \n cousins & friends. Mrs. Dean worked as a teacher's aide at Bancroft School \n & as a coordinator at Piane's Caterers. Her lifelong loves were children, \n family & humor. She was a member of Canaan Baptist Church.",
      "source_url": "https://nativeamericansofdelawarestate.com/Obituaries%20added%202016-04-03.htm"
    }
